<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Types of Gum Infections</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Acute Gingivitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial inflammation of the gums — red, swollen, bleeding gums triggered by plaque accumulation. Reversible with professional cleaning and improved oral hygiene. If left untreated, progresses to periodontitis.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Periodontitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Advanced gum infection destroying the bone and ligaments supporting the teeth. Causes gum recession, tooth mobility, and eventual tooth loss. Requires deep scaling, possible periodontal surgery, and long-term maintenance.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Periodontal Abscess</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A pus-filled gum pocket infection from an existing periodontal pocket becoming acutely infected. Causes intense localized gum pain, swelling, and pus discharge. May require drainage and antibiotics. <a href="painful-gum-swelling-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Painful gum swelling</a> covers this in detail.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Necrotizing Ulcerative Gingivitis (NUG)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A painful, rapidly destructive gum infection with crater-like ulcers between teeth, gray foul-smelling tissue, and spontaneous bleeding. Associated with stress, smoking, and immunosuppression. Requires urgent debridement and antibiotics. <a href="bacterial-mouth-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Bacterial mouth infection</a> covers this.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Pericoronitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Acute gum infection around a partially erupted tooth — most commonly a lower wisdom tooth. The gum flap over the tooth traps food and bacteria, causing pain, swelling, and trismus. May require gum flap removal or wisdom tooth extraction.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Gumboil (Dental Abscess)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">A pus-filled swelling on the gum caused by infection at a tooth root tip — not primarily a gum disease but affects the gum tissue. Requires treatment of the source tooth (root canal or extraction). <a href="pus-in-gums-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Pus in gums</a> and <a href="dental-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">dental abscess</a> pages have full details.</p></div>
